      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Painted enamel on copper is an art of fire, which developed in particular
    during the second half of the 16th century, in the Limoges region of France.
    There, numerous enamelling workshops were set up \u2014 among them one that currently
    goes by the conventional name Oficina da Pequena Paix\xE3o de Santa Cruz de Coimbra
    (Workshop of the Small Passion of the Holy Cross of Coimbra) \u2014 which made
    pieces that were very popular among the elite of the time and were sold around
    Europe."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
